course: dictionary
lesson: 14467
title: Who takes part?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A participant is a person who takes part in something, such as a race, a game, a study or a competition. Look for the word part inside it: a participant is one of the people who are part of the activity.
explain: «Every participant in the race got a medal.» Here, participant means every person who ran in the race. The people cheering from the side are not participants, because they did not take part.
explain: Writers often use the phrases «participants in», «all participants» and «an active participant». An active participant joins in eagerly and fully, not just sitting and watching.
explain: When you meet this word, look at the words around it. If the text describes people doing a game, a test or an event together, participant probably means one of them. Then swap in "person who takes part" to check.
fact: A participant is a person who takes part in an activity, an event, a race, a game, a study or a competition.
fact: Participant is a noun. One person is a participant, and more than one person is participants.
fact: «Participants» can be used in sport, school events, science surveys and maths problems.
fact: «An active participant» means someone who joins in fully and eagerly.
fact: A good check is to swap in "person who takes part": "Every person who took part got a medal" still makes sense, so participant fits.
exercise: «Every participant in the race got a medal.» What is a participant? | A judge who decides the winner | *A person who takes part in the race | A track where runners start | A prize given at the end
exercise: «Ruby was an active participant in the school play.» What does active participant suggest? | Someone who was cross about the play | Someone who lost the script | Someone who only watched from the back | *Someone who joined in fully
exercise: Copy the word that means a person who joins in. | audience | *participant | spectator | crowd
test: «The science survey had 120 participants, put into groups of 8.» How many groups were there? | 8 | *15 | 20 | 12
test: What do the participants in a game do? | *Take part in the game | Watch from the stands only | Clean up after the game | Sell the tickets
exam: Which word means a person who takes part in an event? | judge | *participant | referee | winner
